{"vid":"ScyumiPXca8","source":"ScyumiPXca8.en-GB.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0.2,"txt":"From BBC Learning English."},{"t":2.3,"txt":"This is Learning English from the News, our podcast about the news headlines."},{"t":6.2,"txt":"In this programme,"},{"t":7.4,"txt":"a man lived with a pig's kidney for a record of 271 days."},{"t":17.3,"txt":"Hello, I'm Becca."},{"t":18.4,"txt":"And I'm Phil."},{"t":19.5,"txt":"In this program, we'll look at one big news story"},{"t":22.2,"txt":"and the vocabulary in the headlines that will help you understand it."},{"t":25.6,"txt":"You can find all the vocabulary and headlines from this episode,"},{"t":29,"txt":"as well as a worksheet on our website, bbclearninenglish.com."},{"t":34.2,"txt":"So, let's hear more about this story."},{"t":43.1,"txt":"Tim Andrews from New Hampshire in the United States"},{"t":46.2,"txt":"was aged 66 when he found out"},{"t":48.8,"txt":"that he had developed kidney disease linked to type two diabetes."},{"t":53.5,"txt":"At that time, he was at the end stage of the disease,"},{"t":57,"txt":"meaning that he was in the final, most severe phase."},{"t":60.2,"txt":"Not much can be done at this stage,"},{"t":62,"txt":"and many people in this situation are waiting for a replacement human kidney."},{"t":66.7,"txt":"There is a shortage of human donor kidneys."},{"t":70,"txt":"Andrews received a pig kidney,"},{"t":72,"txt":"and it worked inside him for 271 days, the longest on record,"},{"t":77.7,"txt":"US doctors say."},{"t":79,"txt":"However, the pig organ eventually failed and was removed,"},{"t":82.7,"txt":"so Andrews needed some dialysis, a medical treatment"},{"t":85.4,"txt":"where a machine functions like a kidney."},{"t":88.2,"txt":"He then received a human kidney transplant 82 days later."},{"t":92.7,"txt":"Let's have our first headline."},{"t":94.7,"txt":"Pig kidneys successfully transplanted into humans."},{"t":98.4,"txt":"And that's from the Financial Times, a British newspaper."},{"t":101.6,"txt":"That headline again from the Financial Times."},{"t":104.2,"txt":"Pig kidneys successfully transplanted into humans."},{"t":108,"txt":"So, this headline talks about kidney transplants from pigs"},{"t":111.9,"txt":"and we're going to look at the word transplant."},{"t":114.9,"txt":"What can you tell us about this word, Becca?"},{"t":117.5,"txt":"Well, this word could be both a noun and a verb."},{"t":120.9,"txt":"You can have a transplant or you can transplant something,"},{"t":125.2,"txt":"and it means to move or be moved from one place to another."},{"t":129.9,"txt":"Yes. So, notice there that the stress is different in the verb and the noun."},{"t":134.4,"txt":"So, the verb is transplant and the noun is transplant."},{"t":140,"txt":"Yes, it's often used in a medical context,"},{"t":142.8,"txt":"and it means to take an organ or tissue from one body and put it into another."},{"t":148,"txt":"And in this story, a kidney was taken from a pig"},{"t":151.2,"txt":"and transplanted into Andrews,"},{"t":153.5,"txt":"and a later human organ transplanted into him again."},{"t":157.2,"txt":"And you might also hear transplant when talking about moving plants,"},{"t":161.6,"txt":"so a plant can be grown indoors and later transplanted outside"},{"t":165.9,"txt":"when it's the right season."},{"t":167.7,"txt":"Less commonly, we use transplant metaphorically."},{"t":171.1,"txt":"You can move an idea, habit, culture,"},{"t":173.8,"txt":"or structure forward or into something new."},{"t":177.1,"txt":"For example, an author could try to transplant certain themes from horror"},{"t":181.7,"txt":"into a science fiction setting,"},{"t":183.7,"txt":"or a board of directors could try to transplant a business model"},{"t":188,"txt":"into their retail stores."},{"t":191.2,"txt":"We've had transplant, which means move or be moved from one place to another."},{"t":198.5,"txt":"For example, the donor heart was transplanted in a seven-hour operation."},{"t":208.4,"txt":"This is Learning English from the News,"},{"t":210.5,"txt":"our podcast about news headlines."},{"t":212.7,"txt":"Today we're talking about a man's record-breaking pig organ transplant."},{"t":218.6,"txt":"Tim Andrews is a case of xenotransplantation,"},{"t":222.4,"txt":"the transplantation of organs between species."},{"t":225.8,"txt":"Doctors are saying that xenotransplantation could be"},{"t":229.2,"txt":"a way to address the shortage of human donor organs."},{"t":232.6,"txt":"Pig kidneys are similar to those of humans' in size, general structure,"},{"t":237.3,"txt":"and the way they function."},{"t":238.9,"txt":"However, human bodies will usually reject organs from pigs,"},{"t":242.8,"txt":"but in this case,"},{"t":244,"txt":"the pig was genetically modified to make it suitable for human donation."},{"t":248.7,"txt":"People usually only live for a limited time on dialysis,"},{"t":253,"txt":"that's the machine that acts as a kidney."},{"t":255.5,"txt":"It's hoped that using genetically modified pig kidneys"},{"t":258.8,"txt":"will reduce the amount of time people need to spend on dialysis"},{"t":262.5,"txt":"before receiving a human kidney."},{"t":264.9,"txt":"In a CNN documentary, Andrews said"},{"t":267.3,"txt":"that the transplant helped him become strong enough to be independent again."},{"t":271.1,"txt":"He's now able to cook, clean his home and take his dog Cupcake"},{"t":275.7,"txt":"on long walks."},{"t":276.8,"txt":"Let's have another headline."},{"t":279,"txt":"This headline is from Türkiye Today, a Turkish news organisation."},{"t":283.6,"txt":"First-of-it-kind pig kidney keeps US man off dialysis for 271 days."},{"t":290.9,"txt":"And that headline again from Türkiye Today, a Turkish news organisation."},{"t":295,"txt":"First-of-its-kind pig kidney keeps US man off dialysis for 271 days."},{"t":302.5,"txt":"This headline highlights how this transplant is the first of its kind."},{"t":307,"txt":"What does that mean, Phil, first-of-its-kind?"},{"t":310,"txt":"Well, it describes something completely original, unique,"},{"t":313.5,"txt":"and never done or created before."},{"t":315,"txt":"So, because this is the first example of someone surviving long enough"},{"t":318.7,"txt":"on a pig kidney to then receive a human kidney, it's the first of its kind."},{"t":324.2,"txt":"The part 'of its kind' means belonging to the same category, class,"},{"t":328.8,"txt":"or type as something else."},{"t":330.8,"txt":"You might also hear it with other adjectives."},{"t":333.6,"txt":"For example, if something is the last of its kind, there aren't many left."},{"t":338.7,"txt":"Yes, and if something is the best of its kind,"},{"t":341.3,"txt":"it's, well, better than all the other things in its category."},{"t":345.5,"txt":"And another popular phrase is one of a kind which emphasises its uniqueness."},{"t":352.5,"txt":"We've had, first-of-its-kind, completely original,"},{"t":356.4,"txt":"and has never existed or happened before."},{"t":360,"txt":"For example, the city launched a first-of-its-kind"},{"t":363.3,"txt":"electric bus network that runs entirely on solar power."},{"t":370.9,"txt":"This is Learning English from the News from BBC Learning English."},{"t":374.8,"txt":"We're talking about a xenotransplantation."},{"t":378.1,"txt":"Yes, doctors hope that xenotransplantation"},{"t":381.1,"txt":"of genetically modified pig kidneys could help keep people alive"},{"t":385.4,"txt":"until they can receive a human kidney transplant."},{"t":388.9,"txt":"And this is what our next headline is about."},{"t":391.9,"txt":"Man lived with pig kidney as 'bridge' before human transplant"},{"t":396.4,"txt":"And that's from Euro News, a European news organisation."},{"t":400.3,"txt":"That headline again from Euro News,"},{"t":402.5,"txt":"Man lived with pig kidney as 'bridge' before human transplant"},{"t":407.4,"txt":"So this headline says the pig kidney acted as a 'bridge'"},{"t":411.2,"txt":"before the man received a human transplant."},{"t":413.5,"txt":"And what does that mean here, a bridge?"},{"t":416.4,"txt":"Well, if you think about an actual bridge that you walk across,"},{"t":420.3,"txt":"it supports your weight and gets you from one side to the other."},{"t":424,"txt":"In this medical context, a bridge is a temporary solution"},{"t":428.4,"txt":"that helps someone get from one stage to another."},{"t":431.1,"txt":"It's something that supports a patient"},{"t":432.9,"txt":"until a more permanent treatment becomes available."},{"t":435.9,"txt":"In this case, the pig kidney kept the man alive and reduced the amount of time"},{"t":440.6,"txt":"he had to spend on dialysis while he waited for a human kidney transplant."},{"t":445.3,"txt":"So, the pig kidney acted as a bridge to the next stage of his treatment."},{"t":450.1,"txt":"Yes, and we often use bridge in other situations too."},{"t":453.8,"txt":"For example, a short term loan can be a bridge that helps a company"},{"t":457.9,"txt":"until it receives longer term funding."},{"t":460.9,"txt":"We also have this useful expression 'bridge the gap',"},{"t":464,"txt":"which means to help connect two things."},{"t":469.8,"txt":"We've had bridge,"},{"t":471.6,"txt":"a temporary solution that helps someone get from one stage to another."},{"t":476.1,"txt":"For example, her internship acted as a bridge between university"},{"t":480.6,"txt":"and her dream career."},{"t":483.1,"txt":"That's it for this episode of Learning English from the News."},{"t":487,"txt":"We'll be back next week with another news story."},{"t":490.2,"txt":"And if you found this story interesting, we have a health page over"},{"t":494.9,"txt":"on our website, bbclearningengish.com,"},{"t":498.4,"txt":"which you can also find in the notes for this programme."},{"t":501.2,"txt":"Bye for now. Bye."}],"words":[{"t":0.16,"w":"From"},{"t":0.16,"w":"BBC"},{"t":0.16,"w":"Learning"},{"t":0.16,"w":"English."},{"t":2.28,"w":"This"},{"t":2.28,"w":"is"},{"t":2.28,"w":"Learning"},{"t":2.28,"w":"English"},{"t":2.28,"w":"from"},{"t":2.28,"w":"the"},{"t":2.28,"w":"News,"},{"t":2.28,"w":"our"},{"t":2.28,"w":"podcast"},{"t":2.28,"w":"about"},{"t":2.28,"w":"the"},{"t":2.28,"w":"news"},{"t":2.28,"w":"headlines."},{"t":6.24,"w":"In"},{"t":6.24,"w":"this"},{"t":6.24,"w":"programme,"},{"t":7.4,"w":"a"},{"t":7.4,"w":"man"},{"t":7.4,"w":"lived"},{"t":7.4,"w":"with"},{"t":7.4,"w":"a"},{"t":7.4,"w":"pig's"},{"t":7.4,"w":"kidney"},{"t":7.4,"w":"for"},{"t":7.4,"w":"a"},{"t":7.4,"w":"record"},{"t":7.4,"w":"of"},{"t":7.4,"w":"271"},{"t":7.4,"w":"days."},{"t":17.28,"w":"Hello,"},{"t":17.28,"w":"I'm"},{"t":17.28,"w":"Becca."},{"t":18.36,"w":"And"},{"t":18.36,"w":"I'm"},{"t":18.36,"w":"Phil."},{"t":19.52,"w":"In"},{"t":19.52,"w":"this"},{"t":19.52,"w":"program,"},{"t":19.52,"w":"we'll"},{"t":19.52,"w":"look"},{"t":19.52,"w":"at"},{"t":19.52,"w":"one"},{"t":19.52,"w":"big"},{"t":19.52,"w":"news"},{"t":19.52,"w":"story"},{"t":22.2,"w":"and"},{"t":22.2,"w":"the"},{"t":22.2,"w":"vocabulary"},{"t":22.2,"w":"in"},{"t":22.2,"w":"the"},{"t":22.2,"w":"headlines"},{"t":22.2,"w":"that"},{"t":22.2,"w":"will"},{"t":22.2,"w":"help"},{"t":22.2,"w":"you"},{"t":22.2,"w":"understand"},{"t":22.2,"w":"it."},{"t":25.6,"w":"You"},{"t":25.6,"w":"can"},{"t":25.6,"w":"find"},{"t":25.6,"w":"all"},{"t":25.6,"w":"the"},{"t":25.6,"w":"vocabulary"},{"t":25.6,"w":"and"},{"t":25.6,"w":"headlines"},{"t":25.6,"w":"from"},{"t":25.6,"w":"this"},{"t":25.6,"w":"episode,"},{"t":29.04,"w":"as"},{"t":29.04,"w":"well"},{"t":29.04,"w":"as"},{"t":29.04,"w":"a"},{"t":29.04,"w":"worksheet"},{"t":29.04,"w":"on"},{"t":29.04,"w":"our"},{"t":29.04,"w":"website,"},{"t":29.04,"w":"bbclearninenglish.com."},{"t":34.2,"w":"So,"},{"t":34.2,"w":"let's"},{"t":34.2,"w":"hear"},{"t":34.2,"w":"more"},{"t":34.2,"w":"about"},{"t":34.2,"w":"this"},{"t":34.2,"w":"story."},{"t":43.08,"w":"Tim"},{"t":43.08,"w":"Andrews"},{"t":43.08,"w":"from"},{"t":43.08,"w":"New"},{"t":43.08,"w":"Hampshire"},{"t":43.08,"w":"in"},{"t":43.08,"w":"the"},{"t":43.08,"w":"United"},{"t":43.08,